@datamoc/mw_retro_audio: third-party material and where it is used

This package is MPL-2.0 (see LICENSE). The following files are written from, or reproduce data of, other projects.
No ROM image and no binary of any other program is part of the package.

src/formats/hsc.ts, src/formats/d00.ts, src/formats/rol.ts
  Re-implementations of the behaviour of the HSC-Tracker, EdLib (D00) and AdLib Visual Composer replayers, written
  after reading the AdPlug source (https://github.com/adplug/adplug, Simon Peter et al., LGPL-2.1-or-later). These three
  files carry the licence LGPL-2.1-or-later (SPDX tag in their headers).

src/formats/rad.ts
  Port of the Reality AdLib Tracker v2.1 replayer, which its author Shayde / Reality released to the public domain
  (as distributed in AdPlug, rad2.cpp).

src/chips/Dx7.ts
  Numerical tables and laws (32 algorithms, envelope rate / level laws, level and rate scaling, velocity table, pitch
  envelope tables, coarse frequency table) taken from "music-synthesizer-for-android"
  (https://github.com/google/music-synthesizer-for-android), Copyright 2012 Google Inc., Apache License 2.0
  (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The engine around them is original.

Test data
  tests/fixtures/lha/*.lzh come from the Lhasa project (https://github.com/fragglet/lhasa, ISC licence).
  The 6502 functional test of Klaus Dormann was downloaded to validate the CPU core and is not stored in the repository
  (it is GPL licensed).

Separate programs, not included
  Hatari (GPL-2.0-or-later) through the separate package "hatari-ym".

Optional speech runtimes and model downloads, not included in the core
  Kokoro-82M-v1.0 by hexgrad, Apache-2.0: https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M
  kokoro-js by hexgrad and contributors, Apache-2.0: https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro
  The optional runtime has its own dependency notices, including its eSpeak-NG phonemizer.
  No model weights are embedded in this package. Preserve upstream license and attribution files when self-hosting.

src/speech/kokoroFrench.ts
  French IPA substitutions adapted to TypeScript from hexgrad/misaki's EspeakG2P, Apache-2.0:
  https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki/blob/main/misaki/espeak.py
  The ff_siwis profile is downloaded from Kokoro-82M-v1.0-ONNX (Apache-2.0), revision 4685882.
  Upstream credits the SIWIS French dataset (CC BY 4.0): https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/2353
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M#creative-commons-attribution

src/node/frenchPhonemizer.ts
  Invokes separately installed Python phonemizer and eSpeak-NG via espeakng-loader in an external process.
  These GPL components and their language data are not linked into or redistributed with this package.

tools/render-kitten-voice.py
  Token vocabulary and model-input recipe adapted from KittenML/KittenTTS 0.8 (Apache-2.0):
  https://github.com/KittenML/KittenTTS/blob/0.8/kittentts/onnx_model.py
  Model and voice files are downloaded separately from KittenML/kitten-tts-nano-0.8-int8 (Apache-2.0).
